{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Three feet.</b> Times: you shall serve Me alone, performing three pilgrimages a year, and you shall come before Me like a servant who brings a gift to his master. Therefore it is written after it, את פני האדון ה' (Exodus 23:17), like לפני האדון ה'. And likewise, ולא יראו פני ריקם (Exodus 23:15). And He mentioned this because there are designated days on which the Gentiles go to their vanities; therefore it is written: you shall celebrate to Me alone." "<b>And the word תחוג.</b> You shall slaughter, as in אסרו חג בעבותים (Psalms 118:27)." "<b>Feet.</b> From the root רגל, for most of them are pedestrians."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The word פעמים at the opening appears to mean 'times' or 'occasions,' though its syntactic role is abrupt; translated literally as positioned.", 1 "The verb form is parsed by Ibn Ezra as you shall slaughter, reading ח-ג-ג as related to slaughtering festival offerings."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:42.450572548Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}